-- title:
--   Level-and-type cut of the generated cuspidal subrepresentation lies in M
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, $D$ a set of elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$, $\xi$ a homomorphism from the full group of idele units to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, $N \neq 0$ an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_F$, and $\tau$ an archimedean type family (for each infinite place $w$ a natural number $\mathrm{card}\,w$ and that many archimedean types at $w$). Write $P$ for the carrier pins `productionPinsOf` built from $D$, from the level family $N \mapsto U(N) = \mathrm{levelOne}(N) \sqcap \ker(\mathrm{glArch})$, from the Hecke generators `heckeGen` at the finite places, and from `adelicBox`; in particular its central subgroup is the whole idele unit group, its measure is the adelic Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ and its additive measure is Haar conditioned on `adelicBox`. Let $V$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of the functions $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F) \to \mathbb{C}$ which is a cuspidal subrepresentation for $(P,\xi)$, i.e. $V$ lies in the $K$-finite cusp submodule and is stable under right translation by elements of $\ker(\mathrm{glArch})$, under right translation by $\mathrm{rowIsometryInclAt}_0(w,k)$ for every infinite place $w$ and every $k$ in the connected row-isometry subgroup of $F_w$, and under right convolution with factorizable test functions that are archimedean bi-finite for some type family. Let $M$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of functions $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F) \to \mathbb{C}$ satisfying three closure properties: (k) $M$ is stable under right translation by $\mathrm{rowIsometryInclAt}_0(w,k)$ for all $w$ and all $k$ in the connected row-isometry subgroup at $w$; (H) for every $g \in \ker(\mathrm{glArch})$ and every finite list $\gamma_1,\dots,\gamma_n$ of elements each of the form $u g u'$ with $u,u' \in U(N)$, such that every element of $U(N)gU(N)$ lies in some $\gamma_i U(N)$ and such that $\gamma_i^{-1}\gamma_j \in U(N)$ forces $i=j$, the function $x \mapsto \sum_i \varphi(x\gamma_i)$ lies in $M$ for every $\varphi$ in $M$ which is moreover right $U(N)$-invariant; (C) for every factorizable test function $f$ that is archimedean bi-finite of type $\tau$ and satisfies $f(ux)=f(x)=f(xu)$ for all $x$ and all $u \in U(N)$, right convolution by $f$ maps $M$ into $M$. The conclusion is that if $W_0$ denotes the infimum of all submodules $W$ that are cuspidal subrepresentations for $(P,\xi)$ and contain $V \sqcap \{\text{right }U(N)\text{-invariants}\} \sqcap \mathrm{archCut}(\tau) \sqcap M$, where $\mathrm{archCut}(\tau) = \bigsqcap_w \bigsqcup_i \mathrm{archTypeSubmoduleAt}(w,\tau_w^i)$, then $W_0 \sqcap \{\text{right }U(N)\text{-invariants}\} \sqcap \mathrm{archCut}(\tau) \le M$.
--
--   This is the algebraic half of the minimality step for cuspidal constituents: the level-$N$, type-$\tau$ cut of the cuspidal subrepresentation generated by cut vectors of $M$ is already contained in $M$, because every projected word in the generating operations of a cuspidal subrepresentation reduces to one of the three cut operations (archimedean translation composed with a Hecke coset sum, or a convolution by a bi-$U(N)$-invariant test function). It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.CuspidalConstituent.inf_eq_bot_or_le_of_isCuspConstituent`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.CuspidalConstituent.inf_eq_bot_or_le_of_isCuspConstituent) in the irreducibility dichotomy for cuspidal constituents.
